# Magebane Lizard's triggered ability is independent of its source (CR 113.7a, 608.2h): with the trigger of Bot2's Mox Jet on the
# stack, Bot2 casts Swords to Plowshares on the Lizard in response (its own trigger goes above it). That second trigger resolves
# first: Mox Pearl, Mox Jet and Swords are 3 noncreature spells, 3 damage (19 -> 16). Swords exiles the Lizard (Bot1 gains 1,
# its power). The first trigger then resolves with the Lizard gone: it still counts 3 and the damage is still dealt by the
# Lizard as it last was (16 -> 13).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Magebane Lizard
Mountain x21

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Swords to Plowshares
Mountain x21

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Magebane Lizard.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Magebane Lizard)
? Stack.Count = 4
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 16
? Bot1.Battlefield.Magebane Lizard.Power = 1
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 21
? Bot2.Life = 16
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 13
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 13
Bot1.Life = 21
Exile =Magebane Lizard
Stack.Count = 0
